From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiago Vignatti <vignatti@google.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:55:29 -0300
Subject: [M150-LTS] Don't rebuild date-time edit fields when layout parameters
 are unchanged.

M150-LTS conflicts:
- third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/forms/date_time_edit_element.cc:
  Resolved conflicts in DateTimeEditBuilder::VisitField() where M150
  uses DateTimeFormat::kFieldType* rather than FieldType::kFieldType*
  (renamed in https://crrev.com/c/8474771).

Original change's description:
> Don't rebuild date-time edit fields when layout parameters are unchanged.
>
> The primary change here is changing DateTimeEditElement::GetLayout to
> return early if the layout parameters are unchanged.  However, this
> change has a number of prerequisites that are also included here:
>
> * Adds default comparison operators to make it possible to compare
>   LayoutParameters objects.
>
> * Moves the needs-millisecond-field information into the
>   LayoutParameters.
>
> * Recompute style when changing values (in cases where, previously,
>   elements were reconstructed, plus SetValueAsDateTimeFieldsState which
>   was likely buggy) so that GetCustomStyleForLayoutObject will rerun
>   when the value changes, since it depends on the value (e.g., setting a
>   different width for 5-digit years).
>
> * Clear cached type-ahead buffers when changing the values (which
>   reconstructing the elements previously did, except in the
>   SetValueAsDateTimeFieldsState case).
>
> Fixed: 565838017
> Change-Id: Ic248053b6731c83db92ba99e110a652acfb1ace0
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464610
> Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: David Baron <dbaron@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707763}

(cherry picked from commit 0e25d492d813c083e39834cd47a7a39e7f253a71)

Fixed: 565838017
Change-Id: Ic248053b6731c83db92ba99e110a652acfb1ace0

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): Element::SetFocused() on this branch
takes (bool, mojom::blink::FocusType) with no BlurEventBehavior
parameter, so the new DateTimeSymbolicFieldElement::SetFocused()
override (which resets the type-ahead session on blur) uses that
two-argument signature.

